<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 10.258 percent from 10.261 percent percent at the previous auction on September 11.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Dec 19, 1996 (Dec 12, 1996)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.258 percent (10.261)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 706.3 million (861.825 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 706.475 million (936.925 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.002-10.289 percent (10.002-10.285)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.002-10.572 percent (10.002-10.500)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 144 (137)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 145 (141)</p>
<p>($1=3.40 pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
